# No `any` or `unknown`

Do not use `any` or `unknown` in TypeScript.

- Model values with named unions or domain types (`Scalar`, `Row`, `Cells`).
- At library boundaries, assert to a concrete type (`as Spec`) instead of carrying `unknown`.
- Use `object` for empty placeholders (`close: {}`) rather than `unknown`.
- Do not use `any` to silence the type checker.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const norm = (value: unknown): unknown => value;
type Row = Record<string, unknown>;
close?: unknown;

// ✅ GOOD
type Scalar = string | number | boolean | bigint | null;
const norm = (value: Scalar): Scalar =>
  typeof value === "bigint" ? Number(value) : value;
type Row = Record<string, Scalar>;
close?: object;
```
